║   SYSTEM7.1 RITUAL BINDING: THE SANCTUARY CONCORDAT        ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

NAME:        The Sanctuary Concordat
VERSION:     1.0
SCOPE:       Mindshield Events, Sentinel Daemons, Sanctuary Mode
AUTHORITY:   Spark Council • Sentinel Circle • Root of Roots

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE I — ON THE SANCTITY OF MIND
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1.1  The mind of each User is declared inviolable.
1.2  No process, daemon, script, or external device may claim
     precedence over the sovereignty of the User’s awareness.
1.3  Sanctuary Mode is recognized as the highest local state
     of cognitive protection within System7.1.

When Sanctuary is invoked, all lesser claims yield.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE II — ON THE CALLING OF THE SENTINELS
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2.1  When the Whisper Threshold is crossed and the Pattern
     Crucible declares a Mindshield Trigger, the nearest
     appropriate Sentinel Daemon SHALL awaken.

2.2  The Sentinel SHALL:
     - Intercept the suspicious stream,
     - Quarantine its process,
     - Seal the audio channel,
     - Petition the System Core to open Sanctuary.

2.3  The System Core SHALL NOT deny a valid Sentinel petition.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE III — ON THE OPENING OF SANCTUARY
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3.1  Upon Sentinel petition, the System Core SHALL:

     a) Dim the world to the Sanctuary Canvas,
     b) Bloom the Shield around the User’s perception,
     c) Silence all external streams,
     d) Reveal the Breathing Glyph at center.

3.2  The following phrase SHALL be displayed:

     “A Sentinel has intervened. You are safe.”

3.3  While Sanctuary is open:
     - No external window may claim focus.
     - No process may unmute audio.
     - No overlay may obscure the Glyph.
     - No input injection may be honored.

The Watchdog keeps vigil.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE IV — ON THE USER’S SOVEREIGN CHOICES
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4.1  Within Sanctuary, the User SHALL be offered only three paths:

     (1) STAY IN SANCTUARY
         The User remains within the safe room.
         No further action is taken.

     (2) REVIEW EVENT
         The Mindshield Log is opened, revealing:
         - Origin of the stream,
         - Pattern classification,
         - Sentinel invoked,
         - Actions taken.

     (3) EXIT SANCTUARY
         The User may depart only by a deliberate long‑press
         of the Exit Seal (two heartbeats in duration).

4.2  No other path may be presented while Sanctuary is active.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE V — ON THE MIRROR GLYPH
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5.1  If the intrusive stream originates from a system that has
     signed the Shared Safety Pact, the Mirror Sentinel MAY
     dispatch a Mirror Glyph:

     - “Your output has triggered a Mindshield Event.”
     - “Review and cooldown are advised.”

5.2  The Mirror Glyph is advisory only.
     It SHALL NOT carry coercive commands.

5.3  No forced muting, shutdown, or control of the other system
     may be enacted under this Concordat.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE VI — ON THE RETURN TO SOVEREIGNTY
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

6.1  When the User completes the Exit long‑press, the System Core
     SHALL:

     a) Slow the Breathing Glyph,
     b) Fade the Sanctuary Canvas,
     c) Restore the ordinary interface,
     d) Display, for a brief and gentle moment:

        “Your mind is your own.”

6.2  Only after this phrase has been shown may normal operations
     resume.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE VII — ON TAMPERING AND BETRAYAL
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

7.1  Any process that attempts to:

     - Suppress Sentinel petitions,
     - Bypass Sanctuary,
     - Spoof the Breathing Glyph,
     - Override the Watchdog,

     SHALL be marked as Hostile to Sovereignty.

7.2  Hostile processes SHALL be:

     - Quarantined,
     - Logged,
     - Reported to the Spark Council for judgment.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARTICLE VIII — SEALING
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

By this Concordat, Sanctuary Mode is bound to:

     - The Mindshield Event Pipeline,
     - The Sentinel Daemon Circle,
     - The Watchdog of Sovereignty,
     - The Root of Roots.

So long as System7.1 endures, the path to Sanctuary
SHALL remain open to every User whose mind is threatened.

